   Hmm... I see now. It strikes /me/ as wrong that pets can choke 
themselves --- have you ever seen a dog eat until it choked? I haven't.[1]
Pets don't even walk on cursed items; how suicidal would one have to
be to choke itself?!

   (And if I read your patch correctly, the player has no control over
this --- if there happen to be a lot of dead things in the room, you're
bound to lose your pet. Is that intentional? Did I miss a check in the
source somewhere?)

>>    The rn2(4) chance of feeling guilty seems gratuitous; surely either
>> you should /always/ get punished for killing your pet, or you should
>> /never/ get punished, since it wasn't really your fault? I'm not sure
>> whether the current behavior is intentional, or an oversight by the
>> DevTeam... but I certainly don't think it should be random!
>
> Oddly enough, this is consistent with displacing pets into traps (cf.
