   Weird. Okay, I'll submit to the DevTeam's wisdom on the randomness.
(But I still think the whole idea of pets choking themselves is wrong.)


>>    castmm() and ucast_wizard_spell() call the function "snprintf()",
>> which doesn't exist on most platforms. You should be using sprintf()
>> with an appropriately sized buffer. (The only thing snprintf() does
>> differently is truncate the output if it runs long, and Nethack players
>> won't tolerate truncated output in the first place!)
>
> Programmer's habit - sprintf is a very bad thing in its lowercase s
> form, but I suppose I have Sprintf available which is much nicer.

   Yeah, I realized after posting that Sprintf was correct. And when you
change one of them, make sure to fix the format-string vulnerability,
which will crash the game if anyone names their pet "100% Awesome".

   I've played two games with the patch so far, and wound up with a
pretty powerful pet in both of them: one MMF from a starting wand of
polymorph, and one mastodon from a later acquisition. I noticed that
the MMF liked to throw daggers at things, which was cool; that's from
the patch, right?  (I don't have much experience with high-powered
pets.)

   One bad thing I noticed was that my MMF would do a lot of this:
"Your MMF picks up a dagger. Your MMF wields a dagger! Your MMF picks
up a throwing spear. Your MMF wields a throwing spear! ..."  Two
problems: She[2] was acting like a vacuum cleaner for throwing weapons,
which seemed unrealistic; and the narration was far too breathless.
("She wields /another/ dagger! Wow!") Maybe pets' messages should be
terminated with periods, not exclamation points.

-Arthur

[1] - Fetch a ball until it hyperventilates, yes. Eat until it
chokes, no.

